<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: First-Time Visitors Choosing a 50cc</h1>
<p>Your first rental bike in a new city sets the tone for the whole trip, and in Hanoi the most common first bike is also the smallest: a 50cc scooter or light motorbike. For first-time visitors, choosing a 50cc is less about engine specs and more about fit: how the bike feels under you, how confident you are in traffic, and how much of the city you actually want to cover each day. This guide walks through that decision honestly. The verified rate for a 50cc rental is 200,000 VND per day, and the shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien is open 09:00 to 21:00 daily so you can sit on bikes and ask questions before committing.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a> and pairs with our guides on <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/50cc-scooter-r
ental-for-beginners-hanoi/">50cc scooter rental for beginners</a> and <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/50cc-vs-125cc-hanoi/">50cc versus 125cc bikes</a>. For what every class of bike costs, see the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a>, and for rental terms in plain language, the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> collects what we answer most at the counter.</p>
<nav class="toc">
